  "title": "Motor imagination and execution with a chronic wireless epidural ECoG BCI (WIMAGINE), one participant with tetraplegia (Pollina et al. 2026)",
  "description": "Chronic wireless epidural ECoG recordings (WIMAGINE implant) from one participant with incomplete tetraplegia performing executed and imagined right-arm reaching and wrist-extension movements, alone or simultaneously. The derivative release contains 32 channels over left primary motor and sensory cortex, band-pass filtered at 1-250 Hz, across eight sessions, with trial event tables. The data accompany a study on decoupling simultaneous motor imagination and execution through orthogonal neural representations, and are repackaged in iEEG-BIDS.",
  "methods_description": "A participant with C6 spinal cord injury, implanted with the WIMAGINE wireless epidural ECoG device (64 electrodes per implant, 32 selected from the left implant), performed or imagined right-arm reaching and wrist-extension movements, singly or simultaneously, while seated in front of a screen with instructions and a progress bar. EMG of extensor digitorum and lateral deltoid monitored execution. Signals were sampled at about 585 Hz and band-pass filtered offline (zero-phase 5th-order Butterworth, 1-250 Hz).",
